 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The possessive carry articles",
   "texto": [
    "In Italian the possessive goes with article: **il mio libro** (my book), **la mia casa** (my house), **i miei amici** (my friends).",
    "The forms: **mio, mia** (mi), **tuo, tua** (tu), **suo, sua** (su). In plural: **miei, tuoi, suoi** and **mie, tue, sue**.",
    "They are in line with what is possessed, not with the owner: **sua sorella** can be «his sister.» or «her sister.»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The exception of the family",
   "texto": [
    "With many kinship names in singular the article: **mio padre**, **mia madre**, **mio fratello**, **mia sorella** is omitted. The rule has exceptions: **loro** carries article (**la loro madre**) and a diminutive or modifier usually carries it (**la mia sorellina**, **il mio caro fratello**).",
    "In plural it is used: **i miei genitori** (my parents), **le mie sorelle** (my sisters)."
   ]
  },
